<!--
    ServiceNow Update Set record-definitions for the ATF test suite
    `x_casemgmt Case Management POC` and its 20 `sys_atf_test_suite_test`
    membership links, inside the scoped application `x_casemgmt`.

    WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (Refine-PR Section 3, directive D3.2): the suite is
    what makes the whole set runnable in ONE action - System Applications >
    Automated Test Framework > Suites > "x_casemgmt Case Management POC" >
    Run Test Suite. Each link carries `abort_on_failure = false`, so one red
    test never masks the verdicts of the others.

    EXECUTION ORDER is 100..2000, matching the ATF 01..ATF 20 numbering:
    ATF 01-07 data model + ACL RBAC matrix, ATF 08-17 the state-machine
    transition matrix (ATF 15-17 are the form-level legs), ATF 18-20 the
    anonymous portal contracts.

    PREREQUISITES FOR RUNNING: `sn_atf.runner.enabled` must be `true`, and a
    browser client test runner must be open at `/atf_test_runner.do` for
    ATF 15-17. Both are instance-level test-harness concerns and are
    deliberately NOT captured into the Update Set. See
    `../docs/PDI_LIMITATIONS_AND_KNOWN_ISSUES.md` (ATF section) for the
    captured suite verdict and the negative-control evidence.

    XML ROOT: `<unload>`, matching `../dashboards/*.xml`, because the file
    carries more than one record.

    IDENTIFIERS: every `<sys_id>` is deterministic (md5 of a stable key) and
    the only references are to records this package itself defines - the suite
    and the twenty tests. No foreign sys_id literal appears in this file.
-->
